            <ArticleTitle>Cowper's syringocele causing painful haematuria in an adult.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>308-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A Cowper's syringocele in an adult is rare. Ten cases are reported in the world literature. The authors report a case of painful haematuria due to the presence of a Cowper's syringocele in an adult. The classification of lesions of the Cowper's gland is discussed together with common symptoms and differential diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
